# M16 — the claim-to-source composite FK narrowed to a single column.
#
# WHAT THE GUARD PROTECTS. canon §7.3 item 2: grounding is RELATIONAL, not an application
# check. `scenario_claim`'s foreign key is over `(source_id, scenario_version_id)` against
# `source (id, scenario_version_id)`, so a claim cannot cite a source attached to a
# different scenario_version. That is the constraint the Slice 4 citation tables extend:
# a citation row carries a composite FK to the whole (version, source, claim) triple, and
# a fabricated citation is therefore unpersistable rather than merely rejected by a check
# somebody has to remember to write.
#
# This mutation keeps the constraint NAME and keeps a foreign key — it only drops the
# version column from both sides. The narrowed version still references a unique column
# (`source`'s primary key), so the schema is valid, the seed still applies (every seeded
# claim cites a source in its own version, so the narrower constraint is satisfied), and
# no CTRL block or posture rule reads `pg_get_constraintdef` for this table. The whole
# difference is that a claim pinned to version B may now cite a source belonging to
# version A — which is precisely the fabricated citation FR-02 exists to make impossible.
#
# WHAT A CAUGHT VERDICT ESTABLISHES. That the cross-version insert is REFUSED and is seen
# to be refused with the specific SQLSTATE and the specific constraint name, rather than
# with "an error" that the claim-id shape check or the confidence domain would also
# produce. The named test also reads the constraint definition back from the catalog, so
# the shape the citation tables will reference is asserted and not assumed.
id: M16
title: scenario_claim's source FK drops scenario_version_id from both sides, so a cross-version citation persists
expect: caught
proves: a fabricated citation is unpersistable by schema constraint, and the constraint shape is observed
expect-test: a fabricated citation is unpersistable: the composite FK rejects a (source_id, scenario_version_id) pair that does not exist

file: supabase/migrations/20261021140700_scenario_content.sql
count: 1
@@FIND
  constraint scenario_claim_source_fk foreign key (source_id, scenario_version_id)
    references public.source (id, scenario_version_id) on delete restrict,
@@REPLACE
  constraint scenario_claim_source_fk foreign key (source_id)
    references public.source (id) on delete restrict,
@@END
